      "description": "Watch Union St. Gilloise vs Zulte Waregem highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 17, 2026. The Jupiler Pro League action continued as two determined sides met on the pitch for a tactical showdown. Fans watched closely as the managers looked to outmaneuver each other in a game where every inch of space was fiercely contested. A Tense Opening in Brussels On August 17, 2026 , Union St. Gilloise hosted Lommel United in a fixture that tested the patience and tactical discipline of both sides. From the opening whistle, it was clear that neither team was willing to yield much ground. The first major incident occurred in the 30th minute when Kevin Mac Allister was shown a yellow card for a mistimed challenge, reflecting the physical nature of the early exchanges. Despite several probing runs into the final third, the first half concluded without a breakthrough as both defenses remained resolute. Tactical Shifts and Defensive Rigor The second half began with both managers looking to break the deadlock through strategic adjustments. In the 62nd minute, Lommel United made the first move, introducing Mateo Biondic and Relebohile Mofokeng for Raul Florucz and Besfort Zeneli . Shortly after, Union St. Gilloise defender Fedde Leysen received a caution in the 68th minute, adding to the growing list of disciplinary actions in a hard-fought contest. The game became a battle of attrition as the midfield remained congested. A Flurry of Changes and Stalemate As the clock ticked toward the final whistle, a massive wave of substitutions hit the pitch in the 71st minute. Union St. Gilloise and Lommel United combined for five changes, including the introduction of Adem Zorgane , Ousseynou Niang , and Nikola Mituljikic . These fresh legs were intended to spark late drama, but the organized defensive lines of both teams prevented any clear-cut chances. Even with late introductions like Kewan Vemba in stoppage time, the match eventually ended in a stalemate, with both sides earning a well-deserved point for their defensive efforts."
